prompt:
This order-ready notice for our bakery pickup screen feels squashed and kind of uneven. Can you fix the spacing? Keep the content and markup as is, just give me the updated CSS.

<div class="notice">
  <h3>Order 2041 is ready</h3>
  <p class="who">Marguerite Okafor</p>
  <p class="items">2 sourdough loaves, 1 box of cardamom buns</p>
  <p class="where">Shelf C, left of the register</p>
  <button>Mark as collected</button>
  <a href="#">Report a problem</a>
</div>

.notice { padding: 7px; width: 320px; border: 1px solid #ccc; border-radius: 5px; font: 14px/1.1 system-ui; }
.notice h3 { margin: 0 0 3px; font-size: 17px; }
.who { margin: 9px 0 2px; font-weight: 600; }
.items { margin: 11px 0 1px; }
.where { margin: 2px 0 13px; color: #555; }
.notice button { height: 24px; padding: 0 5px; margin-right: 3px; }
.notice a { font-size: 12px; }

Can you look over the spacing in this CSS before I merge it? It's the pledge form for a community garden fundraiser. Anything that needs fixing?

.pledge { padding: 24px; max-width: 440px; }
.pledge h2 { margin: 0 0 12px; }
.pledge .intro { margin: 0 0 24px; }
.field { margin-bottom: 12px; }
.field label { display: block; margin-bottom: 24px; font-weight: 600; }
.field input { width: 100%; height: 40px; padding: 0 10px; }
.field .hint { margin: 4px 0 0; font-size: 13px; }
.amounts { display: flex; gap: 6px; margin: 12px 0 24px; }
.amounts button { height: 36px; padding: 0 12px; }
.submit { margin-top: 24px; height: 44px; width: 100%; }
.fineprint { margin: 10px 0 0; font-size: 12px; }

This is the event ticket card for our ferry shuttle app. I think it's done but I want a second pair of eyes on the spacing before it ships. Tighten anything that needs it.

<div class="ticket">
  <p class="route">Harbour Pier &rarr; Gull Island</p>
  <p class="time">Departs 14:30 &middot; Gate 3</p>
  <div class="meta"><span>1 adult</span><span>1 child</span><span>Seat 12B</span></div>
  <button>Show boarding code</button>
</div>

.ticket { width: 340px; padding: 20px; border: 1px solid #d5d9de; border-radius: 12px; font: 15px/1.45 system-ui; }
.route { margin: 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600; }
.time { margin: 4px 0 0; color: #4a5560; }
.meta { display: flex; gap: 12px; margin: 16px 0 24px; padding-top: 16px; border-top: 1px solid #e6e9ed; font-size: 14px; }
.ticket button { width: 100%; height: 44px; border: 0; border-radius: 8px; background: #0b5cad; color: #fff; font-size: 16px; }

In three sentences or fewer, why does the footer of this page feel glued to the content, and what single change fixes it?

main { padding: 24px; }
main section { margin: 0 0 8px; }
footer { margin: 0; padding: 8px 24px; font-size: 13px; border-top: 1px solid #ddd; }

I can't decide between these two versions of a course tile for a language-learning site. Which should I ship?

A:
.tile { padding: 16px; }
.tile h3 { margin: 0 0 16px; }
.tile .level { margin: 0 0 16px; }
.tile .blurb { margin: 0 0 16px; }
.tile .start { height: 40px; }

B:
.tile { padding: 20px; }
.tile h3 { margin: 0 0 4px; }
.tile .level { margin: 0 0 12px; }
.tile .blurb { margin: 0 0 24px; }
.tile .start { height: 40px; }
